Description: Jam OS's GN toolchains, //build/toolchain/jamos:x64 and :host
 Chromium's Linux code built for Jam OS (docs/CR-PLAN.md section 1). The
 target toolchain (custom_toolchain) compiles with Chromium's own clang for
 x86_64-unknown-linux-musl against Jam OS's sysroot (target_sysroot) with
 __jamos__ defined, and links with Jam OS's driver (jamos_link_driver:
 tools/jamos-clang through the port's wrapper, static and
 position-dependent through posix.ld, the program's list as its note).
 GN gives the default toolchain the build's own arguments, so args.gn says
 is_jamos and is_musl (copium's argument), and the host toolchain
 (host_toolchain), Chromium's Linux clang toolchain otherwise, puts them
 back to false and builds against Chromium's Debian sysroot.
 With is_jamos: the executable config gives no -pie; the Rust target for
 x64 on musl is x86_64-unknown-linux-musl, and that triple joins the known
 ones (as Alpine adds its own); libffi (Wayland's) is Jam OS's libffi port,
 a static libffi.a in the sysroot, where Linux takes the sysroot's
 libffi_pic.a; the sysroot's headers are in include/ (as Fuchsia's), not
 usr/include, for the system module map.
Forwarded: not-needed (Jam OS's own toolchain; the -pie and Rust triple
 lines could go upstream with is_musl)
